        "original_id": "2270be49-dad0-524f-ae4b-af3ff5fc9a2b",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: John Rhys-Davies, Timothy Dalton, James Bond\n- Products: The Untouchables, Shōgun, Sliders, Robin of Sherwood, The Living Daylights, I, Claudius\n- Roles: Agent Michael Malone, Pilot Vasco Rodrigues, Professor Maximillian Arturo, King Richard I, General Leonid Pushkin, Macro\n- Topics: television remakes, miniseries, film series\n\nFacts:\n- In 1987, The Living Daylights was released as the fifteenth film in the James Bond film series.\n- In 1987, Timothy Dalton became the first actor to star in The Living Daylights as the fictional MI6 agent James Bond.\n- John Rhys-Davies played General Leonid Pushkin in the James Bond film The Living Daylights.\n- John Rhys-Davies played Macro in I, Claudius.\n- John Rhys-Davies played Pilot Vasco Rodrigues in the miniseries Shōgun.\n- John Rhys-Davies played King Richard I in Robin of Sherwood.\n- John Rhys-Davies played Professor Maximillian Arturo in Sliders.\n- In 1993, John Rhys-Davies played Agent Michael Malone in the remake of the 1950s television series The Untouchables.",
